<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en" class="scroll-smooth" data-astro-cid-sckkx6r4> <head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover"><script>(function(){const themeDefault = "dark";
const themeForce = null;

			(function () {
				let theme = themeForce || themeDefault;
				try {
					const stored = localStorage.getItem('theme');
					theme = themeForce || stored || themeDefault;
				} catch {
					/* localStorage blocked (private mode / ITP) — keep themeForce || themeDefault */
				}
				if (theme === 'dark') document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');
				// Keep the browser / OS UI chrome in sync with the resolved app
				// theme — both at boot and whenever DarkModeToggle flips it (it
				// dispatches a `theme-change` event with the new theme).
				try {
					const meta = document.createElement('meta');
					meta.name = 'theme-color';
					const paint = (t) => { meta.content = t === 'dark' ? '#0E1217' : '#ffffff'; };
					paint(theme);
					document.head.appendChild(meta);
					window.addEventListener('theme-change', (e) => paint(e && e.detail && e.detail.theme));
				} catch {
					/* head not ready / blocked — chrome falls back to the browser default */
				}
			})();
		})();</script><script>
			(function () {
				try {
					const html = document.documentElement;
					const ua = navigator.userAgent;
					const lc = ua.toLowerCase();
					const vendor = (navigator.vendor || '').toLowerCase();
					const platform = (navigator.platform || '');
					const isIOS = /iPad|iPhone|iPod/.test(platform) ||
					            (lc.indexOf('mac') > -1 && 'ontouchend' in document);
					const isEdge = lc.indexOf('edg/') > -1 || lc.indexOf('edge/') > -1;
					const isChrome = !isEdge &&
					               lc.indexOf('chrome') > -1 &&
					               vendor.indexOf('google') > -1 &&
					               lc.indexOf('opr') === -1;
					if (isIOS) html.classList.add('platform-ios');
					else if (isChrome) html.classList.add('platform-chrome');
					else if (isEdge) html.classList.add('platform-edge');
					else html.classList.add('platform-default');
				} catch { /* navigator gone or blocked — leave SSR default visible. */ }
			})();
		</script><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png"><link rel="sitemap" href="/sitemap.xml"><link rel="alternate" type="text/plain" href="/llms.txt" title="LLMs.txt"><link rel="canonical" href="https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/"><title>The Best Local LLM Models to Run in 2026 | daily.dev</title><meta name="description" content="Compare six top local LLM families and choose by memory first, then task—recommendations for 8GB to 48GB+ setups and core use cases."><!-- AI/LLM Discoverability --><meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1"><!-- Theme color (browser / OS UI chrome tint) is injected by the
		     FOUC-safe theme bootstrap above so it tracks the resolved app theme
		     (#0E1217 dark / #ffffff light), not the OS `prefers-color-scheme`. --><!-- Open Graph / Facebook --><meta property="og:type" content="article"><meta property="og:url" content="https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/"><meta property="og:title" content="The Best Local LLM Models to Run in 2026 | daily.dev"><meta property="og:description" content="Compare six top local LLM families and choose by memory first, then task—recommendations for 8GB to 48GB+ setups and core use cases."><meta property="og:image" content="https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZqNrEXpH--/f_auto,q_auto/v1/recruiter-landing/6a3886832902db05ecd7a09f_1782097037669_863ad7af06?_a=BAMAMiB80"><meta property="og:site_name" content="daily.dev"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://daily.dev/#organization","name":"daily.dev","url":"https://daily.dev","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://daily.dev/og-image.png","width":1200,"height":630},"sameAs":["https://twitter.com/dailydotdev","https://www.linkedin.com/company/dailydotdev","https://github.com/dailydotdev","https://www.instagram.com/dailydotdev"]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://daily.dev/#website","url":"https://daily.dev","name":"daily.dev","description":"Free, personalized developer news aggregator. Stay on top of software development news, AI coding tools, and web dev - curated daily from trusted sources.","publisher":{"@id":"https://daily.dev/#organization"},"potentialAction":{"@type":"SearchAction","target":{"@type":"EntryPoint","urlTemplate":"https://daily.dev/search?q={search_term_string}"},"query-input":"required name=search_term_string"}},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/","url":"https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/","name":"The Best Local LLM Models to Run in 2026 | daily.dev","description":"Compare six top local LLM families and choose by memory first, then task—recommendations for 8GB to 48GB+ setups and core use cases.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://daily.dev/#website"},"timeRequired":"PT16M"},{"@type":"Article","@id":"https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/#article","headline":"The Best Local LLM Models to Run in 2026","url":"https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/","datePublished":"2026-06-22","dateModified":"2026-06-22T03:21:22.819Z","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://daily.dev/#website"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://daily.dev/#organization"},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/"},"description":"Compare six top local LLM families and choose by memory first, then task—recommendations for 8GB to 48GB+ setups and core use cases.","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZqNrEXpH--/f_auto,q_auto/v1/recruiter-landing/6a3886832902db05ecd7a09f_1782097037669_863ad7af06?_a=BAMAMiB80"},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Carlos Mendoza"},"timeRequired":"PT16M","potentialAction":{"@type":"ReadAction","target":"https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://daily.dev/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Blog","item":"https://daily.dev/blog/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Trends","item":"https://daily.dev/categories/trends/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"The Best Local LLM Models to Run in 2026","item":"https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/"}]},{"@type":"ItemList","numberOfItems":6,"itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Llama_(language_model)","name":"Llama"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mistral_AI","name":"Mistral"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qwen","name":"Qwen"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"url":"https://www.deepseek.com/en/","name":"DeepSeek"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":5,"url":"https://deepmind.google/models/gemma/","name":"Gemma"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":6,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phi_(language_model)","name":"Phi"}],"@id":"https://daily.dev/blog/best-local-llm-models-run/#itemlist","itemListOrder":"https://schema.org/ItemListOrderAscending"},{"@type":"FAQPage","@context":"https://schema.org","mainEntity":[{"name":"Which local LLM is best for coding?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"text":"<p>The best local LLM for coding in 2026 comes down to one thing: <strong>your hardware</strong>.</p> <p>Right now, <strong>Qwen3</strong> and <strong>DeepSeek</strong> are the main picks. If you want professional-grade coding on a single <strong>24 GB GPU</strong>, look at <strong>Qwen3 32B</strong> or the <strong>DeepSeek-V4</strong> series. If you want a strong middle ground for chat, code help, and refactoring, <strong>Qwen3 14B</strong> is a solid fit. And if your main goal is fast IDE autocomplete, <strong>Codestral 22B</strong> stands out.</p> <p>For agentic workflows, <strong>Devstral</strong> is built for multi-file edits and more autonomous tasks. You can run these locally with <strong>Ollama</strong> or <strong>LM Studio</strong>. For setup help, see our guide on running LLMs locally.</p>","@type":"Answer"}},{"name":"What is the best local model for 8 GB RAM?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"text":"<p>On a machine with <strong>8 GB of RAM</strong> and no GPU, a few solid local picks are <strong>Phi-4-mini</strong>, <strong>Gemma 3 1B</strong>, and <strong>Qwen3 1.7B</strong>. These smaller models are a good fit for basic chat on modest hardware, so you don’t need a high-end setup to get started.</p> <p>If you have an <strong>8 GB GPU</strong>, <strong>Qwen3 8B</strong> is widely seen as the best overall choice for 2026. It strikes a nice balance between reasoning and instruction-following. If you want help getting everything running, check the daily.dev guide on running LLMs locally.</p>","@type":"Answer"}},{"name":"How do I choose between Q4 and Q8?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"text":"<p>Q4 vs. Q8 comes down to a simple trade-off: <strong>output quality vs. hardware limits</strong>.</p> <p><strong>Q4</strong> compresses model weights to about <strong>4 GB for every 7–8 billion parameters</strong>. That makes it a solid fit for machines with less memory, while still holding up well in many day-to-day tasks.</p> <p><strong>Q8</strong> gives you higher precision and gets closer to full-quality output. You’ll notice that most with harder reasoning tasks and coding work. The catch is simple: it needs a lot more VRAM.</p> <p>So the rule of thumb is pretty clear:</p> <ul> <li>Choose <strong>Q4</strong> if you’re working with limited memory and want more room for context.</li> <li>Choose <strong>Q8</strong> if your hardware has enough VRAM and you want better output quality.</li> </ul>","@type":"Answer"}}]}]}</script><meta property="article:published_time" content="2026-06-22"><meta property="article:modified_time" content="2026-06-22T03:21:22.819Z"><meta property="article:author" content="Carlos Mendoza"><meta name="keywords" content="local LLMs, on-device AI, LLM hardware, model quantization, Qwen, DeepSeek, Mistral, Gemma"><!-- Twitter --><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:site" content="@dailydotdev"><meta name="twitter:creator" content="@dailydotdev"><meta name="twitter:title" content="The Best Local LLM Models to Run in 2026 | daily.dev"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Compare six top local LLM families and choose by memory first, then task—recommendations for 8GB to 48GB+ setups and core use cases."><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZqNrEXpH--/f_auto,q_auto/v1/recruiter-landing/6a3886832902db05ecd7a09f_1782097037669_863ad7af06?_a=BAMAMiB80"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://media.